        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Six kilometres on from the gorge the bed has flattened to 24.3 m per km\nand the valley has started to open.**\n\nThe same sized box holds **329** marked destroyed. Less violent ground, and more\nof it built on: downstream in Nuwakot alone\n**1,267 houses** were fully damaged and\n**1,253** partially.\n\n**On the map:** the orange reach · the blue fill is the observed water line\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The middle valley"
        }
      }
    },
