        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "fig-gradient-vs-damage.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**One number explains the three: how steeply the riverbed falls.**\n\n![Bed gradient and bridge losses over the same three reaches](attachment:fig-gradient-vs-damage.png)\n\nSteep bed, fast water, everything on the bank hit by what the water is carrying.\nFlat bed, slow water, a river that spreads instead of scours.\n**15 of 16** bridges went in the\ngorge; **6 of 108** on the plain.\n\nAcross the whole corridor NDRRMA count **41 motorable\nbridges washed away** and 4 damaged.\n\n**On the map:** the three reaches, reddest where the bed is steepest\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Why the three are different"
        }
      }
    },
