        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Every figure here is either measured from the data in this folder or quoted\nfrom a named source with the hour it was published.**\n\n**The human figures, and the timeline**\n\n[NDRRMA Situation Report #01](https://ndrrma.gov.np/mediafiles/rasuwa/Rasuwa_Flood_SitRep_Temp_ENG_01_01092026.pdf), 1 September 2026, 09:00.\nDeaths, missing, rescued, isolation, bridges, schools, health facilities, the\narrival times and the account of the cause all come from it. Those numbers moved\ndaily; [BIPAD](https://bipadportal.gov.np/) carries the current ones.\n\n**The damage mapping**\n\n- [Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/hot_flood_npl) — flood extent, destroyed features, bridges, schools, ODbL 1.0.\n- [Copernicus EMS, EMSR927](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/npl-flood-emsr927) — damage grading, © 2026 European Union.\n- [UNOSAT, FL20260826NPL](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/mudflow-rockflow-impact-assessment-in-rasuwa-nuwakot-districts-bagmati-province-nepal-as-o) — flood extent, detachment zone, barrier lakes.\n\n**The imagery**\n\nSentinel-2, 10 m, openly licensed. Every pass after the flood is 70-90% cloud,\nso each before and after is a median of the cloud-free pixels across several\npasses. Ground that never had a clear look is left as a gap.\n\nThe agencies worked from much sharper pictures — Pléiades Neo and WorldView-3 at\n0.3 m, CARTOSAT-3, SkySat — which are commercial and reserved. The vectors drawn\nfrom them can be shared; the images cannot.\n\n**The channel and the reaches**\n\nMeasured from terrain tiles for [an earlier map of this\nflood](https://github.com/arjxn-py/nepal-flood-26-aug), made in the week before\nany of the damage data existed.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Sources"
        }
      }
    }
